# Known MODERATE/HIGH/CRITICAL npm advisories in dashboard/package-lock.json.
# Read by gate.mjs in the CI supply-chain job. One `GHSA-id@package` per line
# (the advisory in that package only); the rest of the line is a note. A bare
# GHSA id is refused by the gate. A new advisory at moderate or above fails
# CI; so does a listed one that is no longer reported (prune it in the change
# that fixes it).
#
# Recorded 2026-09-30: `npm audit` reported 0 vulnerabilities at any level,
# dev dependencies included, after moving to vite 8 (the vite 5 dev server
# carried GHSA-fx2h-pf6j-xcff, GHSA-4w7w-66w2-5vf9 and GHSA-v6wh-96g9-6wx3,
# and its esbuild GHSA-67mh-4wv8-2f99).
#
# Re-recorded 2026-10-20: that is no longer true. `npm audit` reports 1
# moderate, 0 high, 0 critical, 0 low:
GHSA-698v-4r3x-3vcv@vite  # moderate  vite >=8.3.0 <=8.3.2: launch-editor's escapeCmdArgs() omits % escaping on Windows. Dev-server only (the "open in editor" endpoint of `vite dev`); the built dashboard bundle contains no vite code and CI builds on Linux. npm reports a non-breaking fix: bump vite to >=8.3.3 in dashboard/package.json and its lockfile, then delete this line.
